 perceptions concerning outcome of cataract surgery in dogs</article-title><source>JAVMA</source><year>2006</year><volume>228</volume><fpage>870</fpage><lpage>875</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16536695</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Mellor</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Idiopathic epilepsy in dogs: owners' perspectives on management with phenobarbitone and/or potassium bromide</article-title><source>JSAP</source><year>2006</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>574</fpage><lpage>581</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Byron</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><name><surname>March</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Chew</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>DiBartola</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of Phenylpropanolmine and Pseudoephedrine on the urethral Pressure profile and Continnence scores of Incontinent Female Dogs</article-title><source>JVIM</source><year>2007</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>47</fpage><lpage>53</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1892/0891-6640(2007)21[47:EOPAPO]2.0.CO;2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cranberry</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Harvey</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Owner satisfaction with Limb Amputation in Dogs and Cats</article-title><source>JAAHA</source><year>1988</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>227</fpage><lpage>232</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-gr