ncer QLQ-C30: aquality of life instrumentfor use in international clinical trials in oncology</article-title><source>J Natl Cancer Inst</source><year>1993</year><volume>85</volume><fpage>365</fpage><lpage>76</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8433390</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/jnci/85.5.365</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Allison</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Locker</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Feine</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Quality of life: a dynamic construct</article-title><source>Soc Sci Med</source><year>1997</year><volume>45</volume><fpage>221</fpage><lpage>230</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9225410</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0277-9536(96)00339-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jensen</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Jensen</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Grau</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The relationship between observer-based toxicity scoring and patient assessed symptom severity after treatment for head and neck cancer. A correlative cross sectional study of the DAHANKA toxicity scoring system and the EORTC quality of life questionnaires</article-title><source>Radiotherapy and Oncology</source><year>2006</year><volume>78</volume><fpage>298</fpage><lpage>305</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16524633</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.radonc.2006.02.005</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Innes</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Barr</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title